WEBVTT

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.600
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.400
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:24.080
You are my sun now

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.460
We all go through bad times

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.460
no matter who you are

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.890
So don't go hanging your head and feeling down

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:45.640
Keep your head up until your heart's sky

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:51.030
is clear again

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:56.360
No matter where you are in this world

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:59.870
if you're crying and trembling all alone

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:05.210
I'll search for you, I promise

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.880
Love will show me the way

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:16.720
The sun dreams countless times

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:23.560
Forever and always from the horizon

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:30.900
Its shining light gives energy

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:38.240
After all, you are my sun now

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:57.490
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:02.770
<i>I'm travelling with Jasmine and Barda to take back the gems that were stolen by the Shadow Lord.</i>

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.770
<i>And there are only two gems left!</i>

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.820
<i>However, the Shadow Lord is now hunting for a boy, a man and a wild girl with a black bird.</i>

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:15.400
<i>Why am I the 'wild one', anyway?
Honestly, the Shadow Lord has no taste.</i>

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.300
<i>Our journey is sure to become
more perilous from now on!</i>

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.700
<i>Right now, we're headed to the Maze of the Beast, where the sixth gem is hidden!</i>

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.350
It's already been five days
since we left the mountain.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.800
We should be getting close to the river by now.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.300
I just hope that they won't catch
up to us before that, though.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:46.040
The Shadow Lord has ordered all of his
subordinates to keep their eyes peeled

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.840
for a trio consisting of a boy,
a man, and a wild girl after all.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.600
<i>I'm sorry for not letting you fly freely, Kree...</i>

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.220
Jasmine?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.500
Oh, it was just wood mice...

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:14.000
That really freaked me out...

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.400
This forest is unpleasant...

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.400
The trees here stay silent, but
they are constantly watching us...

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:27.200
The trees, huh? I've also had the impression that we were being watched for the last few days now.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.600
Save me!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.000
Look, over there!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.390
Marie! Marie!!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.810
Marie! Marie!

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.600
Marie! Marie!

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.460
You save the one closest to us, Lief!

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.220
Marie!!
You save the one closest to us, Lief!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:47.260
You save the one closest to us, Lief!

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:47.700
Okay!

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.850
Marie! Marie!

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.860
Marie! Marie!

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.130
Marie! Marie!

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:59.640
Grab onto me and don't let go!

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.300
I fell from our raft...

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.020
Marie was trying to save me, but then...

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.210
Marie's not there!

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.100
She hasn't drowned, has she?
She hasn't died, right?!

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.790
Leave this girl to me. You go help Barda.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:35.500
Right.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.050
I'm Jasmine. What's your name?

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.900
Ida... My name is Ida...

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:46.990
Miss, can you take me away from the river?

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:50.220
I hate it! I don't want to be anywhere
near the Tor River anymore!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.760
I understand. Let's go over here, okay?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.600
Look at her, Lief. She must be
the other girl's twin sister.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:12.700
Why did these kids have to go
and play in the river alone...

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:20.490
To think that such a small girl is
now all alone in this world...

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.420
Don't you dare!!

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.050
Stop!

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.700
It's me!

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.350
Don't you recognise me?

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.150
Those twins are actually Ols... They're Ols!

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.400
You... aren't you Dain?!

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:58.070
Hey, wait!

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.090
Barda!

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:40.620
Shit...!

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:47.000
Aim for its heart! You have to finish it off for sure if you don't want Barda to die!

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.310
I've tried to stab it! But it still won't fall!

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:54.440
Jasmine!

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.590
Now! Stab the right side of its chest!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:59.850
Its heart isn't on its left! It's on the right!

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.620
Barda was lucky...

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.540
If we had come even a moment later,
I don't think he would have made it.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:31.000
You're Doom's friend, Dain, aren't you?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.800
What are you doing out here?

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.920
Make sure you keep Barda warm, Jasmine.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:41.500
After all, those who have been attacked by Ols feel frozen from the inside.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.190
I'm really sorry. Even though you saved us, I...

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.000
He's right... If you weren't there...

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.950
You don't have to force yourself to speak.

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:08.410
Try mixing this honey into your tea.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:12.680
It's very effective in strengthening
you, as well as relieving pain.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:19.750
'Quality Brand, Homemade, Organic, Nurturing, Energising, Yummy'...?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.810
That's a pretty long name for honey.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.010
I guess.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.100
Hey, so what are 'Ols' exactly?

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:49.600
They're monsters from the Shadowlands, capable of transforming into anything.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.900
It's not strange to hear that
you guys don't know of them.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:58.900
The Shadow Lord is using them
to commit various evil deeds.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:04.790
They usually come in and out around here; Western Deltora, in other words.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.300
As far as where you guys hail from...

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.500
...that would be from the east, right?

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:22.150
But again, why have you come to this place?

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:25.190
And, how were you able to find us?

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:28.680
I wasn't actually searching
for you guys or anything.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.900
I happened to spot a couple of Ols on my way back to the Resistance's hidden stronghold.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:54.290
So I tailed them, waiting for
my chance to kill them.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.520
And that was when I saw you three.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:03.350
Those accursed Ols were planning to split you up before killing you one by one.

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.150
Had that plan succeeded, you
would likely be dead by now.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:14.770
You're stronger than you look.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:18.500
Well, Doom trained me personally after all.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:26.050
You well and truly saved us, Dain.
You have my thanks for that.

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:30.900
And please forgive us for being suspicious of you.

00:10:31.670 --> 00:10:36.000
It's just that we have become quite used to
being suspicious of others after all this time...

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.200
It's fine. I'm also the same, after all.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.570
Well, I should be going.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:49.550
Take care not to meet any more Ols.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.210
Wait!

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:57.270
Are you really intending on going
through this dangerous place alone?

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.190
Your arm is injured!

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:03.980
There's no need to worry.
Our stronghold isn't that far from here.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:08.750
You should stay here and rest for tonight.
We'll accompany you to your stronghold tomorrow.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:12.700
Lief is right. We can't just turn a
blind eye to an injured person.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.800
You guys sure are kind.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:21.000
Just be careful not to let the
Ols take advantage of it.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:23.880
I'm against this.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.400
I'm completely against letting him stay.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:45.110
Jasmine, I don't really want to spend any more time in this place either.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.100
But if I do nothing,

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:51.800
then I would be letting someone who got injured
because of me go through this dangerous forest alone.

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:53.500
And I couldn't do something like that.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:55.200
But...!

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:58.000
Who's to say we can trust this guy, anyway?!

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:00.900
You're right.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.100
You shouldn't trust others so easily.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:12.100
There are more advanced Ols out there; Ols that are much harder to identify compared to those twins.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:18.200
Take a seat, Dain. And could you please elaborate on what you just said?

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:24.210
Fine. Then I'll take you up on your
kind offer to stay for tonight.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:28.710
And, I'd also like to take you
guys to our hidden stronghold.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:34.350
However, our hidden stronghold in Western
Deltora is actually located south-east from here,

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:38.190
which I believe would be a considerable detour on your journey, right?

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:44.200
How did you know that?! We've never uttered a single word about our destination to you!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.430
Well, that's because...

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:50.000
...I felt that you three were
probably heading to Tora.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:51.350
Tora...

00:12:53.020 --> 00:12:55.240
Oh, you mean the western city of Tora?

00:12:55.240 --> 00:13:00.100
Well, who knows? Even if we are heading to Tora, we still can't go anywhere tonight.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.800
Ols are almost everywhere.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:10.150
They can take the form of anything they please, but they don't eat or drink.

00:13:10.150 --> 00:13:15.000
However, more advanced Ols can
easily just pretend to eat and drink,

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:19.590
and they can even generate body
heat, so they're well disguised.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:26.200
However, regardless of its level, all Ols will have the Shadow Lord's brand on its heart.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:31.800
That's why, no matter what it transforms into, it should have that mark somewhere on its body.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:36.800
Come to think of it, Marie and Ida
did have marks below their eyes...

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.420
Was that it?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.200
Yeah...

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:44.400
But, it won't be that easy to tell when
you're up against the more cunning ones.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.400
Although, there is a surefire way to identify an Ol.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.800
They can't hold their transformation
for more than three days.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:56.600
So, if you observe them for three whole days
without pause, your chance will surely come.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:14:01.100
It will lose its ability to maintain
its form and it will start to waver.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:04.630
We call this phenomenon a Tremor.

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:08.100
A Tremor...

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.000
Yeah...

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:10.900
Dain?

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:12.600
Are you in pain?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.730
You should just rest for tonight.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:17.600
Thanks...

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:19.300
I'll do that.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.430
Are you alright, Dain?!

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:29.880
What's wrong?

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:32.650
We should let Dain rest for a while.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.670
There's no need, I'm fine.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:39.700
I can rest once we get to the stronghold, and it's only a little further.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:46.380
After we climb this cliff... and pass through a separation between the rocks...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.980
...you'll see three thickets, growing in a straight line...

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:55.820
You'll find the entrance there...
hidden behind a rock...

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.600
And the password is...

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:02.340
Stay with us, Dain!

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.500
Have him drink some honey.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:08.870
Here, this is the last of it.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.550
It's not working...

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:16.220
He said that the Resistance's
stronghold is nearby, right?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.100
I'll carry him there on my back.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.600
This is the separation he mentioned, right?

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:32.140
Look there!

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:35.800
Three thickets... So that
must be the entrance, then.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:38.300
Hey!

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:40.690
We are allies! Please open up!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:45.990
We have brought Dain with us! He's injured, so please let him rest inside!

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.660
What's the password?

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.150
Just call Doom here!

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.200
There's no Doom here!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.100
What is the password?

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.200
If you can't say it then you'll be killed!

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:06.330
We are Doom's acquaintances! And can't you see that we're with your comrade right now?!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.950
Of course I can see it.

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:14.860
Because right now, countless arrows are being aimed at you three. So don't even try to move.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.070
What's wrong with you?!

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.340
Didn't I tell you not to move?!

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:24.220
Then, bring Neridah or Glock!
They are your comrades too, right?

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.420
Those two will recognise our faces for sure!

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:35.210
I see... However, appearances don't mean anything around here. That's why we need a password.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:37.800
A password...

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:41.300
If they have one, then they
probably change it everyday.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:47.880
And if that's the case, then Dain was probably going to look for it <i>after</i> we got here.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.100
Lief?! What are you...?!

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:53.540
Lief!

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.600
You'll only get roasted if you hide in there!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:02.520
The arrows aren't coming! As I thought, there must be a clue around here somewhere!

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.210
Found it!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:11.990
'When Enemies At Pass, Orders Normal.'

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:13.800
Wait a minute...

00:17:15.940 --> 00:17:19.800
What's the matter? So you really
don't know the password, do you?!

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.260
No, I just figured it out.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:25.820
Lief...?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:28.760
The password is...

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.100
'Weapon', right?

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:55.000
So the boy who went adventuring has
returned in this pathetic state, has he?

00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:00.970
But I must say, no one would have expected <i>you</i> to
end up like this, given how cautious you usually are.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:05.350
Come down Thalgus, Petronne!
I'll leave Dain to you two!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.400
Hey, is that you Barda?

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.240
It's been a while.

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.570
An acquaintance of yours?

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:33.610
And here I thought that you had died long ago.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.850
Do you still remember me?

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.390
Jinks...

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.000
I never would have guessed that
we'd meet again in a place like this.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.900
How long are you gonna stand around here for?

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:47.500
We don't want to let the cold air inside, do we?

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:08.800
Everyone, we have guests!

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:12.320
These guys have carried the
injured Dain all the way back here,

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:17.300
after that fool failed pathetically
in that 'big adventure' of his!

00:19:18.230 --> 00:19:21.370
He's not pathetic! He saved us
when we were attacked by Ols!

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.400
Yeah. He was very brave.

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:27.400
Look what we have here... Aren't you guys Birdie and Twig from Bushtown?

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.500
You're Glock, aren't you...

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:39.900
The last time we met was when you were being carried away on a stretcher at the Rithmere Games, wasn't it?

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.400
Tsk.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.940
Seems like someone else has arrived.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:51.580
What's the password?

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.080
Weapon.

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:57.930
Who was the fool who threw
the note on the ground?

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.430
Doom...!

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:03.510
Neridah?!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:10.100
Oh? Can someone tell me why I see three faces that don't belong here?

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.320
It's not like that, Doom...

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:15.900
Dain?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.660
So you've finally returned.

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:23.700
Long time no see, Lief.

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:25.850
H-Hi...

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:30.200
Why exactly were you as much as two, or even three days late in your return?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.700
Where did you wander off to?

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:34.470
I found some Ols in the forest...

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:36.750
...so I tailed after them...

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:37.700
By yourself?

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.490
He saved us from danger, you know?!

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.700
I am asking Dain, not you!

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:48.400
Not only have you disobeyed your orders,

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:53.040
but you have also brought three untested strangers into our hidden stronghold,

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:55.800
thus risking the endangerment of us all.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:56.710
Wait, what?!

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.930
They haven't even been tested yet?!

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:02.780
As if that weren't enough, you even
taught them our secret code...

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.600
That's not true!

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:07.160
I figured out the password by myself!

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:08.190
What?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.730
Naturally, there was a hint.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:14.800
It was the bottle of honey that Dain carries.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:16.700
Quality Brand,

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:17.700
Homemade,

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:18.600
Organic,

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:19.300
Nurturing,

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:20.100
Energising,

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:22.100
and Yummy is written there.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:25.500
Reading the first letters of each, it spells 'QB Honey'.

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:31.620
That's why, if we use the same logic with the note from the thicket, the word 'Weapon' is spelled.

00:21:32.780 --> 00:21:34.100
It's not very complicated.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.100
To think that he could figure it out so easily...

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:41.510
Yes sir.

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:44.600
Hey!

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:45.350
Wait!

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:49.960
W-Why are you doing this?!
Did I say something wrong?!

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:52.150
Save your breath.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:56.360
You've figured out one of
our most closely-kept secrets.

00:21:56.360 --> 00:22:00.570
But more importantly, there is no proof that you guys aren't Ols either.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.310
We're not! This is a mistake!

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:05.860
Bring them to the testing room.

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:06.700
Yes sir.

00:22:07.420 --> 00:22:09.770
I will interrogate them
personally in three days.

00:22:09.770 --> 00:22:10.700
Understood!

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:12.220
Wait a minute here!

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:14.170
Now walk!

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:15.120
What's your problem?!

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:17.300
Stop it! You're seriously mistaken!

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:19.500
He's right! Let me go!

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:20.300
Stop it!

00:22:20.300 --> 00:22:21.090
Get in!

00:22:22.740 --> 00:22:25.810
Please wait! We're not Ols!

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:47.840
How long has it truly been, I wonder?

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:57.770
I've been watching the moon all this time, bathing in its light

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:05.190
As we moved closer, a goddess passed over us

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:14.870
And just like that, my little dream was carried away

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:20.500
I saw you when I looked to the night sky

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:20.540
Now that I think of it, your name was written there too
